WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.050
- Do you wanna be friends?

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:03.258
- No. No interest, whatsoever.
(Sam laughing)

00:00:03.258 --> 00:00:04.850
- Okay.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.050
That's me, Sam.

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:08.550
You're probably wondering how I got here.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.660
Well, it started with a question.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.690
Have you ever noticed
that the older you get

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.740
the harder and scarier it
is to make new friends?

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.880
I decided I wanted to challenge myself

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.780
to make 100 new friends

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:21.670
and then get everyone
to meet up in person.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:25.370
So, I pitched my idea to
Jason at Jubilee, and he said,

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:26.630
- If you can pull it off,

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:27.730
maybe we'll put it on the channel.

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:29.010
- This got me so excited
(Facebook messenger ringing)

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.140
that I called my mom.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:30.973
- You don't go up to random people,

00:00:30.973 --> 00:00:31.920
"Wanna be my friend?"

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.350
You're like a creep-o.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:34.183
- [Sam] Thanks mom.

00:00:34.183 --> 00:00:38.610
But, I was still determined
to make 100 new friends.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:39.620
You guys wanna join our picnic?

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.453
- [Man] Sure dude.

00:00:40.453 --> 00:00:41.475
- No way.
Yeah.

00:00:41.475 --> 00:00:42.809
- That made me so happy.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:43.841
♪ Easy come ♪

00:00:43.841 --> 00:00:44.716
♪ Easy go ♪

00:00:44.716 --> 00:00:45.549
- You're not my friend.

00:00:45.549 --> 00:00:46.382
- You're not gonna get 100 people.

00:00:46.382 --> 00:00:50.970
- I was having nightmares
about people rejecting me.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.688
Who should I talk to first?

00:00:54.688 --> 00:00:56.900
(dramatic music)

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:57.733
Excuse me?

00:00:57.733 --> 00:00:58.566
Do you wanna be friends?

00:00:58.566 --> 00:01:00.855
- No. Sorry I have a meeting.

00:01:00.855 --> 00:01:02.308
- Oh, no sweat, no sweat (laughs).

00:01:02.308 --> 00:01:04.086
(melancholy orchestral music)

00:01:04.086 --> 00:01:05.449
Okay. First no.

00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:06.407
Hey!

00:01:06.407 --> 00:01:07.681
Wanna be friends?

00:01:07.681 --> 00:01:08.920
- Sure.
Jelani.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:09.900
- Jelani, Sam.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:10.733
Nice to meet you, man.
- Nice to meet you.

00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:13.462
- Do you wanna come with me
to talk to another person?

00:01:13.462 --> 00:01:15.430
- Sure.
- Let's go Jelani.

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:16.370
Hello.

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:17.570
Do you wanna be friends?

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.473
- Sorry I'm kinda busy right now.

00:01:19.473 --> 00:01:20.873
- Are you in class?

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:22.843
Okay.

00:01:22.843 --> 00:01:24.240
Hey man! Wanna be friends?

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.168
- Sure.
- Sure.

00:01:25.168 --> 00:01:26.080
- Hell yeah!

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:26.913
New friends!
(group cheering)

00:01:26.913 --> 00:01:27.746
Let's go!

00:01:27.746 --> 00:01:29.179
Hey, do you guys wanna be friends?

00:01:29.179 --> 00:01:30.463
- What do you mean?

00:01:30.463 --> 00:01:32.990
- What do you mean what do
I mean? Friends! Friendship!

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:34.025
- Sure.
- Wanna walk together?

00:01:34.025 --> 00:01:35.100
- Walk together?
- Where do you wanna go?

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.644
- Wherever you guys are going!
(Sarah laughing)

00:01:36.644 --> 00:01:38.056
- I'm Sarah, what's your name?

00:01:38.056 --> 00:01:39.470
- Sarah, nice to meet you. Sam.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:40.303
- Malik.

00:01:40.303 --> 00:01:42.250
- So a little backstory on what I'm doing.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.980
I pitched a show to this
company called Jubilee,

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.907
that does empathy-driven content.

00:01:46.907 --> 00:01:47.970
- I love Jubilee.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:49.026
- Oh, you love Jubilee?
- So much!

00:01:49.026 --> 00:01:49.859
- Okay, sick!

00:01:49.859 --> 00:01:51.520
Basically the show is
called "100 New Friends."

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.140
I ask people, "Wanna be friends?"

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:54.100
Do that 100 times,

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.530
and add them all to a group chat.

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.900
And on Friday, invite
everyone to a little picnic

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:00.660
in the park to watch the sunset.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.707
Would you guys be down?

00:02:01.707 --> 00:02:02.780
- Yeah! I'm so down.
- Yeah, that'd be cool!

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:04.998
- Okay, but first I have questions!

00:02:04.998 --> 00:02:05.831
- Okay.

00:02:05.831 --> 00:02:06.710
- Are you guys friends?

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:07.543
- Yup.
- Yeah.

00:02:07.543 --> 00:02:09.371
- Why?
- So, school gets stressful.

00:02:09.371 --> 00:02:12.070
I was just in my head
thinking about a lot of stuff,

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.210
and Sarah just came up
and checked on me one day.

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:15.201
- Oh!
(Sarah laughing)

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:16.720
(indistinct chatter)
- Sarah!

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.650
When you're most stressed,

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:21.490
that's when you see the
quality of your friendships.

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:24.010
Point to the person I should talk to next.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.060
There we go!

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:26.986
Hello! Do you guys wanna be friends?

00:02:26.986 --> 00:02:28.670
(Dina laughing)
- What's up?

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.720
- Do you guys wanna join this group chat?

00:02:32.134 --> 00:02:33.283
- I'm okay.
- No?

00:02:33.283 --> 00:02:35.074
- This is great. No, this
is great. I need "no"s.

00:02:35.074 --> 00:02:36.280
- Because I think it's gonna rain Friday.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:37.140
- There's nothing wrong

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:38.830
with wanting to keep your
social circles small.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:39.840
Because sometimes, you need to focus

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.420
on the friends you do have to
maintain those relationships.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:43.310
So do you wanna join the group chat?

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:44.362
- I would love to.

00:02:44.362 --> 00:02:45.195
- Sure!

00:02:45.195 --> 00:02:46.028
- Sure.

00:02:46.028 --> 00:02:46.880
- Yeah, you can put me in the group chat.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.726
- Okay. Take you on an adventure with me?

00:02:48.726 --> 00:02:50.090
- Okay!
- If you want to. Can you?

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:50.923
Actually, can you?

00:02:50.923 --> 00:02:51.900
- Yeah! I got time.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.233
- Do you wanna be friends?

00:02:53.233 --> 00:02:54.568
- Sure.

00:02:54.568 --> 00:02:56.940
- Go! Let's go, Malik.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.292
Bam!
- Wait, no way!

00:02:58.292 --> 00:02:59.125
- What? Do you know someone in there?

00:02:59.125 --> 00:03:01.041
- A guy I went on a Tinder date with.

00:03:01.041 --> 00:03:02.287
- No way!
(Sam laughing)

00:03:02.287 --> 00:03:03.710
Did it not go well?

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:05.040
(message sending)

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.530
- Not unwell...
(Georgia laughs)

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:07.662
- Hi! Do you wanna be friends?

00:03:07.662 --> 00:03:08.495
- No thanks.

00:03:08.495 --> 00:03:09.474
- That's okay. That's okay.

00:03:09.474 --> 00:03:11.057
It happens. I literally got rejected,

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:12.127
like, five times.
- Trust me. I'm used to it.

00:03:12.127 --> 00:03:14.475
Trust me. I'm used to auditions.

00:03:14.475 --> 00:03:15.860
Do you want to be friends?

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:16.693
- Sure!

00:03:16.693 --> 00:03:17.526
- [Sam] Really? Okay!

00:03:17.526 --> 00:03:19.280
- I don't know very
many people who go here.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:20.520
It's nice to meet people.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:21.450
- New friends, Mya!

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:22.325
That's what it's about!

00:03:22.325 --> 00:03:24.740
Malik, we're on a hugging basis now.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.450
- Friday?
- Yes, I'll see you Friday!

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.100
That's been 11 interviews so far.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:32.430
Man, it's tiring.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.480
Now I am in The Hill,

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.040
which is where all the dorms are.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:37.948
Hey, do you guys wanna be friends?

00:03:37.948 --> 00:03:38.890
- What?
- What?

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:39.723
- Do you wanna be friends?
- Sure!

00:03:39.723 --> 00:03:40.556
- Sure!
- What about me?

00:03:40.556 --> 00:03:41.870
- We just went up to you
guys and knocked on your door

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:42.946
and was like, "Hey, let's be friends!"

00:03:42.946 --> 00:03:43.904
Like, the first day of college.

00:03:43.904 --> 00:03:45.945
- Just like this!
- Yeah, just like this!

00:03:45.945 --> 00:03:47.460
Can I come in?
- Yeah, of course!

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.640
We went into this bar
and we faked a proposal

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.665
so that they would all buy free drinks.

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:53.498
- What?

00:03:53.498 --> 00:03:55.280
Do you guys wanna be friends?

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.529
- I'm a Gryffindor.

00:03:56.529 --> 00:03:57.575
- I'm a Gryffindor, too.

00:03:57.575 --> 00:03:58.599
- I'm a Gryffindor, too!

00:03:58.599 --> 00:03:59.809
- No way!

00:03:59.809 --> 00:04:00.701
- Hey, you guys wanna be friends?

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:01.787
- Aren't we already friends?

00:04:01.787 --> 00:04:03.245
- That's what I like to hear!

00:04:03.245 --> 00:04:04.520
- She's one of my best friends!

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:06.550
- You know you guys are best friends

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:08.150
when Jane just lights up

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:10.510
and is like, "I'm so excited
to answer this question!"

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:11.545
Yeah, so it's called Jubilee.

00:04:11.545 --> 00:04:12.378
- Oh, okay.

00:04:12.378 --> 00:04:13.340
(Jane gasps)
- Yeah.

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:14.790
Hey, do you wanna be friends?

00:04:16.328 --> 00:04:17.161
- No.

00:04:17.161 --> 00:04:17.994
- Sure.

00:04:17.994 --> 00:04:19.085
- Sure!
- No?

00:04:19.085 --> 00:04:19.918
(buzzard beeping)
Okay.

00:04:19.918 --> 00:04:20.751
- Sure.

00:04:20.751 --> 00:04:21.584
- I think we're good.
(buzzard beeping)

00:04:21.584 --> 00:04:22.491
- Well, I'm not gonna be here.

00:04:22.491 --> 00:04:23.700
- Sunset?
- Oh, I'll be out of town.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:24.533
- Aw, damn.

00:04:24.533 --> 00:04:26.510
Hey, do you guys wanna be friends?

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:27.600
- Right in this moment?

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.639
- Would you mind doing an interview?

00:04:29.639 --> 00:04:31.125
- I would mind.
(woman laughing)

00:04:31.125 --> 00:04:31.958
Unfortunately.

00:04:31.958 --> 00:04:32.990
- Okay.
- I'll have to pass.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:33.899
- No sweat.
- Have a good one!

00:04:33.899 --> 00:04:34.960
- Have a good one!

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.920
I think I'm gonna call
it a day on this one.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.430
I'm super tired.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:42.560
The last couple of
interviews have been rough.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.500
At this point, I felt defeated.

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:47.030
I got almost as many no's as I got yes's,

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:49.490
and even some of those yes's
I wasn't so sure about.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:51.870
- I wonder if it's,
like, people are tired.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:52.777
It's dark.
- Yeah.

00:04:52.777 --> 00:04:55.155
- And so if I was being
approached at night,

00:04:55.155 --> 00:04:58.220
I would probably feel a little
more uncomfortable with it.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:00.210
- Yeah. I want people to come.

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:04.360
I just don't want to get a
pizza, set up a slackline,

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.720
wait for people, and then
just have no one show up.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.650
But why should they show up?

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:10.287
Maybe they don't want a random guy saying,

00:05:10.287 --> 00:05:11.220
"Do you wanna be friends?"

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:13.660
And like am I actually creating connection

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.400
in these five minute conversations?

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.030
Or is each person just
a number to get to 100?

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:20.480
The thought of going back to
this ridiculous challenge,

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:21.340
(Sam exhaling)

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:22.410
it was anxiety inducing.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:26.550
I was having nightmares last night

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:29.980
about people rejecting me.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:32.870
But, I said I was going to do this.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:34.454
So, I started day two.

00:05:34.454 --> 00:05:37.204
(dramatic music)

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:43.640
Hey, do you wanna be friends?
- Sup, man? How are you doing?

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:44.473
- Hello! I'm Sam.
(Andrew laughing)

00:05:44.473 --> 00:05:45.980
- Food is the way to the soul.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:46.977
- Ah, food!

00:05:46.977 --> 00:05:47.810
- Yeah.
(Sam laughs)

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:49.390
- It was my best friend's birthday-

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:50.810
- Yeah.
- And he had COVID.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:51.643
- Oh no!

00:05:51.643 --> 00:05:53.540
- So I literally was
like, "Oh, that sucks!"

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.940
So I picked him up some
food and sat outside

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:57.690
and we ate through a screen door together.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.210
- That's amazing!
- Yeah, it was fun.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.230
We were both in choir together.

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:02.063
- You got some pipes?

00:06:02.063 --> 00:06:02.896
- Yeah!

00:06:02.896 --> 00:06:05.013
♪ I'm just a poor boy ♪

00:06:05.013 --> 00:06:07.472
♪ I need no sympathy ♪

00:06:07.472 --> 00:06:09.863
♪ Easy come, easy go ♪

00:06:09.863 --> 00:06:10.696
(both laughing)

00:06:10.696 --> 00:06:13.770
- Friday at 5:00 PM at Janss Steps.

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:16.130
- I should be good!

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:16.963
I think so!

00:06:16.963 --> 00:06:18.720
- Andrew! I appreciate you, bro!

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:19.810
The biggest hump to get over

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.730
is always that first interaction.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.360
It's so hard but then you get over it,

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:27.260
and then someone
reciprocates and it's fine!

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:28.093
It's like. I'm like, okay.

00:06:28.093 --> 00:06:29.003
Wanna be friends?

00:06:30.056 --> 00:06:31.222
- Sure!
- Yes!

00:06:31.222 --> 00:06:32.055
- Sure.

00:06:32.055 --> 00:06:33.721
- Yeah, let's be friends.
- Bro, I'm friends with him

00:06:33.721 --> 00:06:35.054
because he's one of the best dudes I know.

00:06:35.054 --> 00:06:36.545
- Oh, I got... I have to go.

00:06:36.545 --> 00:06:38.240
- Sure, dude!
- Hell yeah! What's your name?

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:39.073
- Matt.
- Sure!

00:06:39.073 --> 00:06:39.906
(Sam laughing)

00:06:39.906 --> 00:06:40.739
- Yeah
(Sam laughing)

00:06:40.739 --> 00:06:42.734
- They called me "Dr.
Phil." I love to listen.

00:06:42.734 --> 00:06:43.567
Like, do you want a hug?

00:06:43.567 --> 00:06:44.940
I'd rather have that type of person.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:46.110
- Rather than prescribing.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:47.570
Malik!

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:48.530
Straight for the hug!

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:49.760
Who do we wanna talk to first?

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.240
How about this person?

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.567
Hello!

00:06:52.567 --> 00:06:53.655
Do you wanna be friends?

00:06:53.655 --> 00:06:55.422
- I don't know. We have
talk a little bit more.

00:06:55.422 --> 00:06:57.356
- [Sam] Okay. My name's Sam!

00:06:57.356 --> 00:06:58.790
- Nice to meet you.
- Hello.

00:06:58.790 --> 00:06:59.623
This is Malik.

00:06:59.623 --> 00:07:00.620
- Hi, I'm Malik.
- Hi.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:01.960
- What's your name?
- Elena.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:03.290
- Do you mind if we sit?

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:04.340
- Sure.

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:05.560
- Elena, okay.

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:09.123
So, I'm doing a documentary on friendship.

00:07:09.123 --> 00:07:10.840
- That's super cool.
- Thank you!

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.880
- I'm nicer with my friends.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:15.208
- Fair. And not strangers that ask you,

00:07:15.208 --> 00:07:16.223
"Do you wanna be friends?"

00:07:16.223 --> 00:07:17.056
- Yeah.

00:07:17.056 --> 00:07:19.630
I don't understand what the show is.

00:07:19.630 --> 00:07:20.530
Like what the-

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:21.363
- So, great question.

00:07:21.363 --> 00:07:24.580
After COVID, I feel like connection

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.130
has been really hard to come by.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:26.963
- Yeah.

00:07:26.963 --> 00:07:28.410
- I just wanted to show that
you could put effort in,

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:29.940
and then people will show up.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:32.070
And there exists
friendship out of nothing.

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:32.903
- Interesting.

00:07:32.903 --> 00:07:34.350
"Friendship" and
"friendship out of nothing"

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:35.990
are different themes for a documentary.

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:38.940
- It's friendship out of
nothing, initially, right?

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:39.880
Initially, when I approach you,

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:40.920
I don't know who you are.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:42.520
But the minimum, I guess,

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:44.570
is can you be friendly back?

