00:15:41.532 --> 00:15:43.342
This is Andrew, the opera singer.

00:15:43.342 --> 00:15:44.758
- Hi guys.
- Hi Andrew!

00:15:44.758 --> 00:15:46.380
- He has amazing pipes.
(Sam laughs)

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:48.030
What made you wanna come out out?

00:15:49.450 --> 00:15:51.060
- Well, because I've been actually

00:15:51.060 --> 00:15:51.893
having a really shitty week.

00:15:51.893 --> 00:15:54.307
I had to put down one
of my pets on Monday.

00:15:54.307 --> 00:15:55.970
So, just having a rough one,

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:59.224
and I needed to get a little
out of my comfort zone.

00:15:59.224 --> 00:16:00.890
Meet some new people.
- Yeah.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:03.393
That's what this is for.

00:16:03.393 --> 00:16:05.640
- I'll be honest, I'm
surprised by the turnout.

00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:06.830
- COVID, it's been hard.

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:07.690
- Oh, yeah.
- A lot of people.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:10.398
- I found that I got way too comfortable

00:16:10.398 --> 00:16:11.680
with how things were.

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:13.038
Like, during COVID times.

00:16:13.038 --> 00:16:16.413
I used to be super
outgoing, talk to anybody

00:16:16.413 --> 00:16:17.246
and then COVID happened.

00:16:17.246 --> 00:16:20.359
And you kinda just lose the
will to go out and make friends

00:16:20.359 --> 00:16:22.212
but hopefully we're heading back towards

00:16:22.212 --> 00:16:23.624
a semblance of normalcy.
- Yeah.

00:16:23.624 --> 00:16:24.457
All right, you ready?

00:16:24.457 --> 00:16:26.030
- I don't know.
- Okay, here.

00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:27.963
Take my hand, and then put it up.

00:16:29.399 --> 00:16:32.571
You got it. You got it. You
got it! Three, two, one!

00:16:32.571 --> 00:16:34.600
(woman wailing)

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:36.837
- You need leg strength
for this, don't you?

00:16:36.837 --> 00:16:38.920
- There we go! There we go!
One, thanks for showing up,

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:40.587
but also thanks for opening up.

00:16:40.587 --> 00:16:41.795
I appreciate that.
- Yeah!

00:16:41.795 --> 00:16:43.135
We need a little bit more of that.

00:16:43.135 --> 00:16:44.093
- Are you happy?

00:16:44.093 --> 00:16:45.233
- I'm so happy.

00:16:45.233 --> 00:16:47.883
- Yeah. Is it all working
out how you wanted it to?

00:16:47.883 --> 00:16:49.390
- [Sam] I think so. It's like-

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:50.723
It feels special.

00:16:50.723 --> 00:16:52.181
- Yeah. I'm so glad!

00:16:52.181 --> 00:16:54.022
(indistinct chatter)

00:16:54.022 --> 00:16:55.921
Aw, I'm so happy I met you!

00:16:55.921 --> 00:16:57.600
- I'm so happy I met you, too.
- You make me so happy!

00:16:57.600 --> 00:16:58.433
- What's your name?
- Jyrhed.

00:16:58.433 --> 00:17:00.150
- Jyrhed, nice to meet you!

00:17:00.150 --> 00:17:00.983
Jyrhed said yes!

00:17:00.983 --> 00:17:03.520
(mouse clicks)

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:04.401
(upbeat music)

00:17:04.401 --> 00:17:05.620
- Engineers!
- I know, bro!

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:07.830
- We got extra canvases
if you want to paint too.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:09.417
- Dude, actually, so down!

00:17:09.417 --> 00:17:11.827
Jyrhed, I appreciate you!

00:17:11.827 --> 00:17:14.074
All right, and then Angie,
as soon as you get in!

00:17:14.074 --> 00:17:16.570
(indistinct chatter)

00:17:16.570 --> 00:17:18.432
Three, two, one!

00:17:18.432 --> 00:17:20.946
- [Everyone] 100 New Friends!

00:17:20.946 --> 00:17:23.877
(friends cheering)

00:17:23.877 --> 00:17:26.420
- [Sam] So, was this whole
experiment a success?

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:29.670
Part of me says, "Sam,
you asked 162 people

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:32.271
to come to a picnic, 52 people said no,

00:17:32.271 --> 00:17:34.870
only 11 came and you cheated

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:38.440
and grabbed 20 at the
last second, you failed."

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:40.681
But, the other part of me says, "Wow!

00:17:40.681 --> 00:17:43.800
110 people said yes to being friends

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:45.210
and joining a group chat."

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:46.180
Better than that,

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:48.610
there were 11 people
who completely changed

00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:51.730
the course of their day to
come to a random picnic.

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:54.480
All these people saw the
possibility of friendship

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:57.460
in a brief interaction
and took the first steps

00:17:57.460 --> 00:18:00.030
towards creating a
relationship of substance.

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:01.630
Looking back on this experiment,

00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:04.150
it wasn't really about
making 100 new friends,

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:07.480
it was about trying 100
times, knowing that I'd fail.

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:09.430
But, if I tried hard enough,

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:12.000
a few real friendships could blossom.

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.200
This was hard, but, I loved it.

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:16.896
And I think that's what
makes life beautiful.

00:18:16.896 --> 00:18:19.393
And I'm really excited
to explore this more.

00:18:20.763 --> 00:18:23.156
(Sam laughing)

00:18:23.156 --> 00:18:24.906
This was really cool.

00:18:28.637 --> 00:18:29.470
All right.

